# [[.Title]]

A Steward plugin for [[.Title]], built with the [Go SDK](https://github.com/treno-dev/steward/tree/main/sdk/plugin/go).

## Run

```sh
go mod tidy
go run .
```

Steward starts the plugin itself and talks to it over gRPC. Running it by hand prints the handshake
line the runner reads, and nothing else on standard output. Write logs to stderr.

## Where things are

`main.go` declares the integration (what it needs to connect), each kind of resource and the handlers
Steward calls: `Provision`, `Deprovision`, `GrantAccess`, `RevokeAccess` and `GetAccess`. Handlers take
and return the typed messages of the contract. Leave out the handlers you do not need: Steward offers
only what you implement.

To add a kind of resource, call `plugin.Resource(steward.ResourceKind{...})` again with its own inputs,
outputs and handlers.

See the [SDK README](https://github.com/treno-dev/steward/blob/main/sdk/plugin/go/README.md) for
everything a plugin can declare.
